### Final commit
\`5da167bc98324b7beaaf5e076dd150c34268d377\` — \"Neon Threader: playable game with final screenshots\" on branch \`opencode/34075619354\` (pushed, no PR per instructions).

### Deployment status
- Local app server (tmux \`app-server\`, port 3000): HTTP 200, serves \`index.html\`.
- Public URL above: HTTP 200, full browser suite re-ran green against it.

### Test status (playwright-core + Chromium, public URL)
ALL_CHECKS_PASSED, zero pageerror/console errors: start screen visible, canvas present, Start->play, keyboard steering collected a spark (score 0->10), P pause/resume, wall hit->game-over screen, R->play score 0. Earlier fix: inline data-URI favicon eliminated a favicon 404.

### Known limitations
- Tron-style constant motion: the thread never stops, so new players can hit a wall within ~2s of spawn if they don't steer immediately.
- Trail self-collision only activates once the trail exceeds 45 points, so tight instant reversals early in a run are forgiven.
- Canvas backing store caps DPR at 2; audio/sound effects are not implemented." && gh issue view 51 --comments | tail -8
